        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Traditional Stone Cottage with Panoramic Sea Views – Binghamstown, Belmullet, Co. Mayo\r\n\r\nNestled down a peaceful country lane in the picturesque village of Binghamstown, this traditional stone cottage offers a rare opportunity to restore and create a truly special home in one of North Mayo's most scenic coastal settings.\r\n\r\nEnjoying panoramic views across Emlybeg South and Broadhaven Bay, the property is set in an idyllic location where the beauty of the Atlantic coastline can be appreciated from your doorstep. Just 5 minutes' drive from Belmullet town, the property combines the tranquillity of rural living with the convenience of nearby shops, schools, restaurants and local amenities.\r\n\r\nThe cottage offers enormous potential for renovation and modernisation, allowing the new owner to preserve its traditional character while creating a stunning coastal residence or holiday retreat. Adding to its appeal is an original stone barn located adjacent to the cottage, offering further potential for storage, workshop space or conversion (subject to the necessary planning permission).\r\n\r\nSituated along the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way, this property is surrounded by beautiful beaches, rugged coastline and endless opportunities for walking, fishing and outdoor pursuits.\r\n\r\nWhether you're looking for a restoration project, a holiday home or a peaceful permanent residence, this charming cottage presents an exceptional opportunity to create something truly unique."
